WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.000
This programme contains
some strong language and violence.

2
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.176
You said that this was encrypted
inside the BT malware?

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.240
Yeah.

4
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.176
Well. you have a date.
a time and a place.

5
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.216
It looks like someone's sending us
an invitation.

6
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.856
I think someone should go to Harrogate.

7
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.560
Me. if no-one else will.

8
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.216
OK.

9
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.096
And you better go with her.
If it's Cyber World.

10
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.936
the FSB are gonna be there. It's
likely one of their provocations.

11
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.256
It's got all the hallmarks.

12
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.256
According to our embassy in Moscow.

13
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.256
the lights have been flashing
on and off in Putin's office.

14
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:41.696
What do you need?

15
00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.336
The Jolly Roger?

16
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.816
He blames Russia for the attack

17
00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:48.999
and he says that he's retaliating.
Calls himself a "patriotic hacker".

18
00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.560
You speak good English. I think.

19
00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:11.440
Do you wanna de-compress?

20
00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.040
S-Sure.

21
00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.616
It's not... It's not a good idea.

22
00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.496
You're upset.

23
00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:27.656
There is something you
haven't found yet. something hidden.

24
00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:30.256
What? There's nothing else -
we've checked. Listen.

25
00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:33.296
It's really dangerous.
It could cause a war.

26
00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:36.096
You can stop it. Look in the malware.

27
00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.136
Please don't tell my name. not to anyone.

28
00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:42.120
If they find out I told you this.
they will kill me.

29
00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:51.880
Danny can see us in 45.

30
00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.456
I'll meet you there.
We don't wanna be late.

31
00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.176
I'll meet you there. OK?

32
00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.560
Sure.

33
00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:09.016
Hey. stranger.
I thought you'd gone to Harrogate.

34
00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.976
Just got back.

35
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.056
I'm on my way to work. but...

36
00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.176
I wanted to see you.

37
00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.840
Great.

38
00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:22.600
Go on. sir!

39
00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:32.960
So. what was he like?

40
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.496
Like?

41
00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:38.239
Yeah. What did you make of him?

42
00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:45.336
He was young. About my age.

43
00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.920
Dressed in a hoody.

44
00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:51.640
He was... He was frightened.

45
00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:54.496
Like he was...

46
00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:57.016
And you'd never seen him before?

47
00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:58.600
No. Never.

48
00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:03.520
What should we do?

49
00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.400
About his warning?

50
00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.576
Something else hidden in the code.

51
00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:11.640
That's right.

52
00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:15.600
What do you think?

53
00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:23.200
I guess that I trust Saara's
instincts. She's been right before.

54
00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.656
It feels like a provocation to me.

55
00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:32.816
It's classic FSB mind games.

56
00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.816
It's very vague.

57
00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:37.576
Nothing specific. nothing we can use.

58
00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:38.896
Resources are tight. you know.

59
00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.296
I can't keep throwing people
at this thing. you know.

60
00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.920
Not without something concrete to go on.

61
00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:50.176
Look. if you want to keep looking.
that's fine. all right?

62
00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.496
But in your own time. OK?

63
00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.800
OK. I better run.

64
00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.560
That's it? Apparently.

65
00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:07.160
Hey. What?

66
00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.480
Do you wanna get a drink after work?

67
00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.816
Look... what happened in Harrogate -

68
00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:21.160
it was a mistake. OK?

69
00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:27.056
I don't usually drink alcohol and I...

70
00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.880
It was a mistake. That's all.

71
00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:30.960
Sure.

72
00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.776
How much do you know
about what we do here?

73
00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.536
Just what I've read online.

74
00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:59.376
That we're Putin's poodle.
A propaganda mouthpiece.

75
00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.776
Of course the people who say that
mostly work

76
00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:04.496
for media billionaires and publish
what they're told to publish.

77
00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:06.216
So glass houses. wouldn't you say?

78
00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:09.296
Or maybe you don't know that
English expression? No. I know it.

79
00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:12.736
Steve Cleary.
one of our shooting producers.

80
00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:16.336
Hi. Rad tebya videt. I'm afraid
that's the only Russian I know.

81
00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:18.776
Nice to meet you too.

82
00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:19.896
You ready to get out there?

83
00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.136
Now?

84
00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:23.536
Sure. Why not? Just do what he says.

85
00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:26.576
He knows what he's doing. More or less.

86
00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:27.600
OK.

87
00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:43.496
Are you Daz? That's right.

88
00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:46.536
Thanks for coming.
I'm Kathy. Can I join you?

89
00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:47.640
Be my guest.

90
00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:54.336
I'm told you were mentioned at
Cobr recently.

91
00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:56.056
Really?

92
00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:58.216
Did they enjoy my Russian light show?

93
00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:00.216
I think it got their attention.

94
00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:03.176
And Putin's. probably. It's hard
to undermine the free world

95
00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.480
when the lights in your office
are literally on the blink.

96
00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:09.200
Apparently some people thought
that it was us.

97
00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.576
Is that right?

98
00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.096
Well...

99
00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:15.656
you only have to ask.

100
00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:18.016
You know what?

101
00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:20.680
That is exactly what I've been sent
to talk to you about.

102
00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:24.776
I thought GCHQ didn't employ
black hats.

103
00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:29.976
Well. maybe not employ. exactly.
More of an informal contribution.

104
00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.296
On what basis?

105
00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.920
On a patriotic basis.

106
00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.056
That's how you describe yourself. isn't it?

107
00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.856
Jolly Roger the Patriotic Hacker?

108
00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:39.976
Even patriots get paid. Kathy.

109
00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.160
I'm sure we can come to
an arrangement.

110
00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:05.856
This is it? This is it.

111
00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:08.656
Vote Labour. Vote Labour.

112
00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:10.480
Vote Labour. Thanks very much. Cheers.

113
00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:14.016
Put them on.

114
00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:15.536
You're joking right?

115
00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:17.656
No. I'm not joking.

116
00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:19.416
I'm not in any danger.

117
00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:20.600
Just do it. OK?

118
00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:33.760
Who are they?

119
00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:47.176
Now.

120
00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:49.896
I never thought I'd have to dress
in full riot gear

121
00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:53.216
here on the streets of the UK.
But with this general election

122
00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:54.856
just days away...

123
00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:56.080
Again.

124
00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:00.736
I never thought I'd have
to dress in full riot gear.

125
00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:02.936
here on the streets of the UK.

126
00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:04.936
But with this critical general...

127
00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:08.376
election just days away.
confrontations like this

128
00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:11.016
are becoming more and more common.

129
00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:13.776
There. That's great. with the glass
breaking. Use that. Yeah.

130
00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:15.736
We want an end to immigration.

131
00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:17.816
But they don't care about democracy
or free speech.

132
00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:18.896
What's she saying?

133
00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:21.096
"Only electing a white populist regime

134
00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:23.576
"can put an end to this chaos."
blah-blah-blah.

135
00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.600
OK. great. We'll take that.
Have you got a good end shot?

136
00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:29.120
The girl.

137
00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:34.416
Perfect. Great.

138
00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:36.816
Upload that and e-mail me
the metrics when they're in.

139
00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:38.120
Great job. Marina.

140
00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:45.216
Excuse me.

141
00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:46.360
Angie.

142
00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:49.296
Steve - how did he know?

143
00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:50.776
Know what?

144
00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:54.376
He gave me the riot gear
before there was any violence.

145
00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.336
He knew it was going to happen.

146
00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:59.240
Did we organise
that counter-demonstration?

147
00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:02.200
We organised both of them.

148
00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:06.480
What? Come on.

149
00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:16.696
Right. Facebook page for
Luton For Labour.

150
00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:19.256
set up seven months ago. by us.

151
00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.136
We tweet about it with our fake accounts

152
00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:24.176
and then the bots retweet it
thousands of times.

153
00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.656
And then like-minded people sign up.

154
00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:30.096
So it doesn't exist.
Luton For Labour? You made it up?

155
00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:33.776
Well. it exists. on this page.
It's got 96 members.

156
00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:36.736
And here's the message
in the diary about today's event.

157
00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:37.976
Put there by you?

158
00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.656
That's right.

159
00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:44.536
OK? And here's the Facebook page

160
00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:47.016
for Take Back Control Of Luton.

161
00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:50.816
a fascist group that think it's time
we went back to the 1930s.

162
00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:52.360
also set up by us.

163
00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:55.896
And here's a message
about a protest today.

164
00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:58.936
at the same time. on the same street.

165
00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:00.016
So they all turn up.

166
00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:02.736
completely unaware
there's gonna be a rival group.

167
00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:05.816
and then as soon as they see
each other. they clash.

168
00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:08.016
There's no need for us
to provoke on the ground.

169
00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.856
If we've attracted the right kind of people.

170
00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:11.320
it'll kick off of its own accord.

171
00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:15.856
So it's all made up. The whole thing.

172
00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:17.960
Well. I prefer "managed".

173
00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:23.736
But what's the point
of reporting something

174
00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:26.856
that's so obviously fake news?

175
00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:29.616
Look. you need to forget all your
previous experience

176
00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:33.896
as a journalist. OK?
Whether it's faked isn't the point.

177
00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:37.040
I mean. everything that's reported
is fake. one way or another.

178
00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:39.496
We know people won't believe it.

179
00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:42.296
It probably contradicts what we said
yesterday. It doesn't matter.

180
00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:47.336
The point is to get people used to
the idea that everything's a lie.

181
00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:49.176
that there is no truth.

182
00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:51.456
And once they accept that...

183
00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:54.120
well. biggest liar wins.

184
00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:05.160
Shit.

185
00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:25.400
Christ!

186
00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:43.120
Where did you get all this stuff?

187
00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:46.216
Back of a skip.

188
00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:48.616
When they were clearing out... Oakley.

189
00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:49.920
Is that for Morse code?

190
00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:56.616
I'm... I'm sorry.
I'm interrupting your meal.

191
00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:59.800
No. here. here. Here. have a seat.

192
00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:08.200
Here. Try it.

193
00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:15.576
Good?

194
00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:17.336
I-I can't...

195
00:14:17.360 --> 00:14:18.520
Sorry.

196
00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:49.336
Have a go. Go on.

197
00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:50.800
Me?

198
00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:02.576
How was that?

199
00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:04.960
Borderline crap.

200
00:15:09.240 --> 00:15:13.256
This must all seem
very. very old-fashioned to you.

201
00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:16.336
but this was... This one -
this was state-of-the-art.

202
00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:19.376
State-of-the-art in its day.

203
00:15:19.400 --> 00:15:20.816
You nicked it. didn't you?

204
00:15:20.840 --> 00:15:22.096
No.

205
00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:24.336
No. no. I told you.

206
00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:26.600
I found it. Back of a skip.

207
00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:29.840
Where you found me.

208
00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:40.520
I haven't got very much.

209
00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:49.120
But if you come barging in uninvited
you have to take your chances.

210
00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:53.240
Like I say. I'm really not hungry.

211
00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:57.096
You'll eat what you're given...

212
00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:58.960
and you'll enjoy it.

213
00:16:11.720 --> 00:16:13.576
It's really good.

214
00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:16.016
You needn't sound so surprised.

215
00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:20.936
Anyhow. my brilliant
analytical mastermind

216
00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:24.936
deduces that you didn't come here
for the pleasure of my company.

217
00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:27.880
Come on - spit it out...
if you see what I mean.

218
00:16:29.080 --> 00:16:32.216
You're gonna tell me I shouldn't
discuss this with you.

219
00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:34.616
Compartmentation and all that.

220
00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:35.640
Probably.

221
00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:39.360
OK.

222
00:16:41.360 --> 00:16:45.496
I think there's something else
hidden in the BT malware.

223
00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:46.896
A third stage.

224
00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:49.760
And your suspicions
aren't widely shared?

225
00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:55.456
Everyone thought I was so clever.

226
00:16:55.480 --> 00:16:57.240
finding the hidden level.

227
00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:04.176
But... I'm wondering if we weren't
meant to find it.

228
00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:05.760
so that we didn't look any further.

229
00:17:07.600 --> 00:17:10.520
I think maybe there's something else
hidden in there.

230
00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:15.576
It's the Nigerian prince.

231
00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:19.336
What? You get an e-mail from
a Nigerian Prince.

232
00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:24.456
He has �50 million and he wants to
deposit it in your account.

233
00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.096
Hurrah. What do you do?

234
00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:28.536
Delete it. It's spam.
Everyone knows that.

235
00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:29.600
Exactly.

236
00:17:30.720 --> 00:17:33.576
As soon as you see an e-mail
from a Nigerian prince.

237
00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:37.336
without even opening it.
you think it's spam.

238
00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:42.856
Trouble is. the other side knows...
that's what you're going to think.

239
00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:45.416
The Russians are always
looking at probabilities -

240
00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:48.616
they adore working out
how one behaviour leads to

241
00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:51.000
another predictable behaviour.

242
00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:55.496
They've been studying us.
how we behave.

243
00:17:55.520 --> 00:17:58.176
since... Well. since before the war.

244
00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:01.919
Sounds like you admire them -
the Russians.

245
00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:06.320
No. I don't admire them.

246
00:18:08.120 --> 00:18:11.360
I respect them. as worthy adversaries.

247
00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:15.056
So. what are you saying?

248
00:18:15.080 --> 00:18:16.336
What am I saying? I'm saying.

249
00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:21.056
yes. what if the other side has
already predicted

250
00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:24.896
every step you'll take
when you analyse the malware?

251
00:18:24.920 --> 00:18:28.656
OK. fine. but how does that help?

252
00:18:28.680 --> 00:18:29.896
It's a mountain of code.

253
00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:32.256
I still have no idea where to start.

254
00:18:32.280 --> 00:18:34.816
Dear.

255
00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:37.440
"A mountain of code."
Do you mind if I...?

256
00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:43.416
Perhaps it will make you
check your assumptions.

257
00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:45.976
Remember the Nigerian prince.

258
00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:48.376
If you find yourself scouring through

259
00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:51.856
thousands and thousands
of lines of code.

260
00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:53.760
that's probably...

261
00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:57.736
exactly what they're expecting you to do.

262
00:18:57.760 --> 00:18:59.136
Don't.

263
00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:01.400
Do something else. unexpected.

264
00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:04.680
OK.

265
00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:06.880
Like what?

266
00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:10.536
Check the comms.

267
00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:13.776
Find out how it's communicating
and you're halfway there.

268
00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:16.856
But it doesn't. That's the point.

269
00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:19.736
This malware doesn't beacon at all.

270
00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:22.856
Well. I suspect it's how
you define communicating.

271
00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:25.240
Everything communicates.
one way or another.

272
00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:31.240
You'll have to think outside the box.

273
00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:40.920
And. if you can't. then you have
to find someone... who can.

274
00:19:47.560 --> 00:19:49.216
Aha.

275
00:19:49.240 --> 00:19:50.896
Well. I don't know. I...

276
00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:54.479
I think there's life in the old dog yet.

277
00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:08.576
Hey.

278
00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:10.616
You still here?

279
00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:13.840
Working on the BT malware...
in my own time.

280
00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:17.840
So. what you doing?

281
00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:25.880
Questioning our assumptions.

282
00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:28.720
You've lost me.

283
00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:31.160
Everything.

284
00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:33.840
What we think its purpose is.

285
00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:37.400
Whether it communicates
with the outside world.

286
00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:41.656
I thought it didn't communicate.

287
00:20:41.680 --> 00:20:42.856
Exactly.

288
00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:44.440
That's one of our assumptions.

289
00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:49.960
Another is that it didn't run
in the sandbox.

290
00:20:51.280 --> 00:20:52.879
I'm gonna try again.

291
00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:06.400
Anything?

292
00:22:11.440 --> 00:22:13.400
Hey. It was worth a try.

293
00:22:17.560 --> 00:22:20.840
Why didn't he say anything else?
In Harrogate?

294
00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:24.120
Why couldn't he be more specific?

295
00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:30.600
Maybe he didn't know.

296
00:22:33.600 --> 00:22:36.696
Or maybe Danny IS right

297
00:22:36.720 --> 00:22:40.056
and it's just another provocation.

298
00:22:40.080 --> 00:22:42.376
Another way to fuck with us -

299
00:22:42.400 --> 00:22:45.456
tie us in knots looking for
something that doesn't exist?

300
00:22:45.480 --> 00:22:48.096
I don't know. I don't know
what I'm doing any more.

301
00:22:48.120 --> 00:22:49.360
Yes. you do.

302
00:22:50.920 --> 00:22:53.600
That is about the only thing
that is for sure here.

303
00:22:56.200 --> 00:22:57.600
You were born for this.

304
00:23:03.960 --> 00:23:05.400
Don't stay too late.

305
00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:41.920
You're not convinced. are you?

306
00:23:45.880 --> 00:23:48.176
Why did you bring me over here?

307
00:23:48.200 --> 00:23:49.280
Don't you know?

308
00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:52.040
No. actually. I don't.

309
00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:04.200
I read this.

310
00:24:06.480 --> 00:24:07.640
Tell me why you wrote it.

311
00:24:09.040 --> 00:24:10.520
To cause trouble.

312
00:24:11.560 --> 00:24:13.040
No. I don't think so.

313
00:24:14.240 --> 00:24:17.056
I think you were trying
to make Russia a better place.

314
00:24:17.080 --> 00:24:18.616
Really?

315
00:24:18.640 --> 00:24:20.456
Yeah. I think so.

316
00:24:20.480 --> 00:24:23.560
And you risked your liberty and the
safety of your daughter to do it.

317
00:24:25.040 --> 00:24:27.920
I think you're a patriot. but you
probably don't like to admit it.

318
00:24:29.440 --> 00:24:33.600
That's what I'm trying to do here -
make Britain a better place.

319
00:24:35.200 --> 00:24:38.336
But you're supporting Putin.

320
00:24:38.360 --> 00:24:39.840
And we were criticising him.

321
00:24:41.320 --> 00:24:42.576
Well. we're taking his money.

322
00:24:42.600 --> 00:24:44.280
It's not necessarily the same thing.

323
00:24:46.280 --> 00:24:48.456
Look. it's very simple.

324
00:24:48.480 --> 00:24:51.256
You pointed out everything that was
wrong with your society

325
00:24:51.280 --> 00:24:52.576
and you were very good at it.

326
00:24:52.600 --> 00:24:54.520
And I want you to do
the same thing here.

327
00:24:57.360 --> 00:25:02.336
But Putin wants to trample all over
Britain. not reform it.

328
00:25:02.360 --> 00:25:04.176
No. he doesn't.

329
00:25:04.200 --> 00:25:07.856
He wants to overturn the world order
and he's right.

330
00:25:07.880 --> 00:25:10.376
Russia has to get out from under
the domination of the West

331
00:25:10.400 --> 00:25:11.856
if it's gonna grow.

332
00:25:11.880 --> 00:25:14.976
And we have to tear apart what
we've got here. from the inside.

333
00:25:15.000 --> 00:25:16.920
so we can build again. better.

334
00:25:30.600 --> 00:25:32.680
Why can't I come in the front entrance?

335
00:25:35.560 --> 00:25:38.800
Our staff would be uncomfortable.
having you in the building.

336
00:25:41.280 --> 00:25:45.680
Why? Do I have "black hat" tattooed
on my forehead?

337
00:26:01.320 --> 00:26:02.576
Wait for me here.

338
00:26:02.600 --> 00:26:05.776
What? Why? How long will you be?

339
00:26:05.800 --> 00:26:07.000
I don't know.

340
00:26:24.320 --> 00:26:27.120
Hey. Can I borrow her for a minute?

341
00:26:29.520 --> 00:26:31.880
Sure.

342
00:26:47.200 --> 00:26:49.640
You know that we've been hunting
the BT coders?

343
00:26:51.560 --> 00:26:52.600
You found them?

344
00:26:56.480 --> 00:26:59.640
The guy you met in Harrogate -
is he one of these?

345
00:27:09.160 --> 00:27:11.200
No. No.

346
00:27:14.800 --> 00:27:16.920
Please. This is really important.

347
00:27:25.400 --> 00:27:26.480
I promised.

348
00:27:28.160 --> 00:27:30.000
I promised I wouldn't identify him.

349
00:27:32.480 --> 00:27:35.640
He said his life would be in danger.
I told you. he was terrified.

350
00:27:37.720 --> 00:27:41.136
Well. we're about to publish their
names and photographs.

351
00:27:41.160 --> 00:27:44.216
You're what? Why?

352
00:27:44.240 --> 00:27:46.256
As part of our response to the attack -

353
00:27:46.280 --> 00:27:47.680
to show that Russia was behind it.

354
00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:50.616
Not him. Please.

355
00:27:50.640 --> 00:27:53.120
We have to protect him. I promised him.

356
00:27:54.720 --> 00:27:55.760
Who?

357
00:27:58.200 --> 00:27:59.440
Who. Saara?

358
00:28:11.840 --> 00:28:13.240
Vadim Trusov.

359
00:28:15.280 --> 00:28:17.536
Yeah.

360
00:28:17.560 --> 00:28:18.920
How do you know?

361
00:28:21.400 --> 00:28:25.736
I went to uni with him.
That's how I know he's genuine.

362
00:28:25.760 --> 00:28:27.976
Please don't do anything to hurt him.

363
00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:31.920
I don't care about the others
but don't expose him. Please.

364
00:28:33.080 --> 00:28:35.296
That would be even worse for him -

365
00:28:35.320 --> 00:28:36.936
if we expose everyone else but not him.

366
00:28:36.960 --> 00:28:39.096
it's just gonna throw suspicion on him.

367
00:28:39.120 --> 00:28:42.176
It's gonna make it look like he's a
British spy. What. so

368
00:28:42.200 --> 00:28:44.896
this is everyone - the whole team?
Is that what you're saying?

369
00:28:44.920 --> 00:28:47.136
No. but... So why can't he be
one of the ones you miss out?

370
00:28:47.160 --> 00:28:48.336
Because he's a key player.

371
00:28:48.360 --> 00:28:51.016
If he's not there
it's gonna look really suspicious.

372
00:28:51.040 --> 00:28:54.320
It's actually safer for him if he's
exposed as part of the group.

373
00:29:00.600 --> 00:29:01.960
Saara?

374
00:29:05.000 --> 00:29:06.640
He'll think I've betrayed him.

375
00:29:19.080 --> 00:29:20.640
Are you OK?

376
00:29:33.440 --> 00:29:36.096
Can I say something? Yeah. of course.

377
00:29:36.120 --> 00:29:37.696
Doesn't this make it more likely

378
00:29:37.720 --> 00:29:40.216
that what he told her in Harrogate
was true?

379
00:29:40.240 --> 00:29:42.096
Vadim.

380
00:29:42.120 --> 00:29:43.976
Well. he's one of the coders.

381
00:29:44.000 --> 00:29:46.896
They wouldn't risk someone like
that on a provocation operation.

382
00:29:46.920 --> 00:29:48.496
would they?

383
00:29:48.520 --> 00:29:50.576
They'd just send someone expendable.

384
00:29:50.600 --> 00:29:51.720
Someone like me.

385
00:29:55.440 --> 00:29:59.376
Unless... they knew their coder
was at college

386
00:29:59.400 --> 00:30:01.456
with someone from our
malware department.

387
00:30:01.480 --> 00:30:04.560
so that sending him would make their
provocation more believable.

388
00:30:05.960 --> 00:30:09.696
Yeah. But how could they know that?

389
00:30:09.720 --> 00:30:11.296
That she worked here? And also.

390
00:30:11.320 --> 00:30:13.800
they had no idea who was
gonna turn up. did they?

391
00:30:17.160 --> 00:30:21.016
But even if what he says is true.
where does that get us?

392
00:30:21.040 --> 00:30:23.816
I've had every hacker in this
building tear this code apart

393
00:30:23.840 --> 00:30:25.840
and there's nothing. It's a dead end.

394
00:30:31.520 --> 00:30:35.280
So... should I give them all
to Jolly Roger - him included?

395
00:30:40.480 --> 00:30:42.680
Yeah. Do it.

396
00:30:48.400 --> 00:30:50.416
All good? Fine.

397
00:30:50.440 --> 00:30:51.560
OK.

398
00:30:57.920 --> 00:31:00.136
Sorry to keep you waiting.

399
00:31:00.160 --> 00:31:02.736
Positions of power and influence.

400
00:31:02.760 --> 00:31:06.496
One of the men named by the
Jolly Roger website is Vadim Trusov.

401
00:31:06.520 --> 00:31:10.160
the son of Felix and Ludmilla
Trusov. owners of the Russ...

402
00:31:19.480 --> 00:31:21.536
You're gonna have to explain this to me.

403
00:31:21.560 --> 00:31:23.560
How Vadim's any different
from you or me.

404
00:31:25.040 --> 00:31:27.216
He does what he's told
because it's his job.

405
00:31:27.240 --> 00:31:28.600
just like you and me.

406
00:31:30.120 --> 00:31:32.776
Yes. There is a difference.

407
00:31:32.800 --> 00:31:34.576
He took a massive risk to try to help us.

408
00:31:34.600 --> 00:31:36.840
whereas you and I
just threw him to the wolves.

409
00:31:38.040 --> 00:31:39.896
Saara...

410
00:31:39.920 --> 00:31:41.256
Jeremy...

411
00:31:41.280 --> 00:31:45.096
This Jolly Roger - who is he?
See what you can find out.

412
00:31:45.120 --> 00:31:47.376
Is he a front for the spooks?
Does he even exist?

413
00:31:47.400 --> 00:31:48.416
Quick as you can. yeah?

414
00:31:48.440 --> 00:31:50.840
And prep a background piece
on everything else he's done.

415
00:31:58.800 --> 00:32:00.376
Angie.

416
00:32:00.400 --> 00:32:02.680
What? Can I speak to you?

417
00:32:10.760 --> 00:32:13.696
I'd like to try for an interview...

418
00:32:13.720 --> 00:32:15.816
with one of the coders.

419
00:32:15.840 --> 00:32:18.096
The bids are already in.
Might happen. Might not.

420
00:32:18.120 --> 00:32:20.176
Depends which way they wanna play it.

421
00:32:20.200 --> 00:32:22.920
Anyway. it's a job for
one of the presenters. No offence.

422
00:32:24.080 --> 00:32:25.840
I may have another way in.

423
00:32:27.520 --> 00:32:30.240
I think Vadim Trusov would talk to me.

424
00:32:31.520 --> 00:32:33.136
Why?

425
00:32:33.160 --> 00:32:34.720
We're friends.

426
00:32:57.320 --> 00:32:58.600
Hiya.

427
00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:07.736
Hi. Tell me you're not going into
work now.

428
00:33:07.760 --> 00:33:09.319
Yeah. 'fraid so.

429
00:33:13.680 --> 00:33:16.280
What are you looking at?

430
00:33:31.680 --> 00:33:34.456
You guys not gonna do anything?
No can do. mate.

431
00:33:34.480 --> 00:33:36.319
It's a police-free zone. innit?

432
00:33:45.480 --> 00:33:47.040
Can you hold that?

433
00:38:26.040 --> 00:38:27.600
You ready?

434
00:38:29.760 --> 00:38:30.880
OK.

435
00:38:41.720 --> 00:38:42.800
OK?

436
00:38:44.800 --> 00:38:46.680
You know you can do this.

437
00:38:48.520 --> 00:38:49.880
Thank you.

438
00:39:18.720 --> 00:39:21.656
Mr Trusov.
you're accused of being behind

439
00:39:21.680 --> 00:39:24.536
the cyber-attack that caused
billions of dollars of damage

440
00:39:24.560 --> 00:39:25.816
to another nation.

441
00:39:25.840 --> 00:39:27.976
What's your response
to these allegations?

442
00:39:28.000 --> 00:39:29.920
I had nothing to do with this.

443
00:39:30.960 --> 00:39:35.696
What about the evidence offered by
the Jolly Roger website?

444
00:39:35.720 --> 00:39:37.720
It's incontrovertible. isn't it?

445
00:39:39.240 --> 00:39:40.376
What can I say?

446
00:39:40.400 --> 00:39:43.496
I'm a computer engineer
working in cybersecurity.

447
00:39:43.520 --> 00:39:46.296
I know absolutely nothing about this.

448
00:39:46.320 --> 00:39:48.216
Your parents.
Felix and Ludmilla Trusov...

449
00:39:48.240 --> 00:39:50.736
I don't have anything
to do with my parents.

450
00:39:50.760 --> 00:39:53.536
I make my own way in the world.

451
00:39:53.560 --> 00:39:56.256
Maybe that's why I was targeted -
because of my parents.

452
00:39:56.280 --> 00:39:57.680
I don't know.

453
00:39:59.000 --> 00:40:02.416
What about these people...

454
00:40:02.440 --> 00:40:04.520
who are accused alongside you?

455
00:40:07.640 --> 00:40:10.240
I've never seen them before in my life.

456
00:40:16.720 --> 00:40:20.056
So. to your knowledge you had never
before met anyone.

457
00:40:20.080 --> 00:40:22.456
dealt with anyone. from the FSB?

458
00:40:22.480 --> 00:40:24.176
Is that what you're saying?

459
00:40:24.200 --> 00:40:25.816
No.

460
00:40:25.840 --> 00:40:27.160
Not until yesterday.

461
00:40:29.320 --> 00:40:32.776
You met the FSB yesterday? Why?

462
00:40:32.800 --> 00:40:35.416
They had something for me.

463
00:40:35.440 --> 00:40:37.496
What did they have for you?

464
00:40:37.520 --> 00:40:39.616
Information.

465
00:40:39.640 --> 00:40:41.616
Information?

466
00:40:41.640 --> 00:40:43.896
About the people who did this to me.

467
00:40:43.920 --> 00:40:47.256
About the people who tried
to ruin my life.

468
00:40:47.280 --> 00:40:48.400
What people?

469
00:40:50.040 --> 00:40:52.136
One of them is an analyst

470
00:40:52.160 --> 00:40:56.256
at the UK's
intelligence organisation. GCHQ.

471
00:40:56.280 --> 00:40:59.216
She's on secondment from
the National Security Agency

472
00:40:59.240 --> 00:41:00.616
in the US.

473
00:41:00.640 --> 00:41:05.376
The other is an illegal hacker
who works as a freelance for GCHQ.

474
00:41:05.400 --> 00:41:07.720
known as Jolly Roger.

475
00:41:13.560 --> 00:41:16.560
The analyst's name is Kathy Freeman.

476
00:41:20.720 --> 00:41:24.336
The hacker is Darran Wiskowski.

477
00:41:24.360 --> 00:41:26.640
Their addresses are written there.

478
00:41:32.880 --> 00:41:34.880
So. can you explain how you...

479
00:42:06.720 --> 00:42:09.056
The other is an illegal hacker

480
00:42:09.080 --> 00:42:11.216
who works as a freelance for GCHQ.

481
00:42:11.240 --> 00:42:13.120
known as Jolly Roger.

482
00:42:18.040 --> 00:42:21.240
The analyst's name is Kathy Freeman.

483
00:42:47.960 --> 00:42:50.160
You still think that
he was just doing his job?

484
00:43:25.960 --> 00:43:28.440
I've had to search
the whole building to find you.

485
00:43:37.800 --> 00:43:40.056
So...

486
00:43:40.080 --> 00:43:41.120
are you leaving?

487
00:43:43.640 --> 00:43:44.840
I haven't decided.

488
00:43:46.320 --> 00:43:47.480
But are you safe here?

489
00:43:49.080 --> 00:43:51.080
What about your flat?
Won't you have to move out?

490
00:43:52.240 --> 00:43:53.880
Danny's getting me packed up.

491
00:43:56.560 --> 00:43:58.200
They'll find me somewhere else.

492
00:44:00.640 --> 00:44:02.880
You could stay with us.

493
00:44:04.440 --> 00:44:06.056
I mean. it's really tiny.

494
00:44:06.080 --> 00:44:07.880
You'd have to sleep on the sofa.

495
00:44:09.760 --> 00:44:11.120
But it's safe.

496
00:44:18.320 --> 00:44:19.440
Bedroom.

497
00:44:20.640 --> 00:44:22.216
It's cute.

498
00:44:22.240 --> 00:44:23.320
Yeah.

499
00:44:25.080 --> 00:44:27.696
And then there's a dining table.

500
00:44:27.720 --> 00:44:29.280
and then this is the kitchen.

501
00:44:32.160 --> 00:44:34.536
You're welcome to use
the fridge. stove. oven -

502
00:44:34.560 --> 00:44:37.200
anything. Thanks.

503
00:44:40.760 --> 00:44:42.520
Like I say. it's small.

504
00:44:43.680 --> 00:44:46.136
It'll only be for a couple of days.

505
00:44:46.160 --> 00:44:47.639
Stay as long as you need.

506
00:44:54.040 --> 00:44:57.200
My God. What happened?

507
00:45:01.040 --> 00:45:02.080
That's you.

508
00:45:03.360 --> 00:45:04.816
We work together.

509
00:45:04.840 --> 00:45:07.576
She needs somewhere safe to stay.

510
00:45:07.600 --> 00:45:09.520
I said she could stay here.

511
00:45:13.560 --> 00:45:15.096
OK.

512
00:45:15.120 --> 00:45:16.656
What happened?

513
00:45:16.680 --> 00:45:19.416
We were...

514
00:45:19.440 --> 00:45:21.760
We were attacked on the protest.

515
00:45:24.840 --> 00:45:26.656
I was arrested.

516
00:45:26.680 --> 00:45:29.856
God! Yeah. James. are you OK?

517
00:45:29.880 --> 00:45:31.656
I should go.

518
00:45:31.680 --> 00:45:33.696
No. no. She asked you to stay.

519
00:45:33.720 --> 00:45:35.320
Stay.

520
00:45:40.400 --> 00:45:43.120
So. what happens now?
Will they want to retaliate?

521
00:45:44.600 --> 00:45:45.640
Possibly.

522
00:45:47.280 --> 00:45:48.616
I think we're more worried

523
00:45:48.640 --> 00:45:51.256
about what Russia's got planned
for the election.

524
00:45:51.280 --> 00:45:54.416
God knows what else they've got
squirrel led away in our systems.

525
00:45:54.440 --> 00:45:57.720
Yeah. but another retaliation
can't be the answer. can it?

526
00:46:00.960 --> 00:46:03.216
Outing our analyst was just
them retaliating

527
00:46:03.240 --> 00:46:04.576
for us naming their coders.

528
00:46:04.600 --> 00:46:08.536
If we attack them again.
